\fs57\fsmilli28708 \cf2 Background\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 So what sorts of traits are characteristic of higher reading levels? Well, longer words probably correlate with higher reading levels. Likewise, longer sentences probably correlate with higher reading levels, too.\
A number of \'93readability tests\'94 have been developed over the years that define formulas for computing the reading level of a text. One such readability test is the Coleman-Liau index. The Coleman-Liau index of a text is designed to output that (U.S.) grade level that is needed to understand some text. The formula is\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs28 \cf2 \cb6 index = 0.0588 * L - 0.296 * S - 15.8\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 where 
\f1\fs28 L
\f0\fs32  is the average number of letters per 100 words in the text, and 
\f1\fs28 S
\f0\fs32  is the average number of sentences per 100 words in the text.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

